del_id IS the meter size. Not needed.\n\nOne more consideration: should the model_level instead be config_level with axis \"meter_size\"? Rule 5 says config axes are for configurations, not models. DN size is part of model designation, so model_level is right.\n\nmatrix_tables rows: I'll use arrays for meter_size groups. Hmm, but schema example rows use scalars. Arrays are valid JSON and truthful. Alternatively string \"DN40, DN50\". I'll go with arrays — clearer.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether to include both model_level (28×3) and matrix_tables (7 rows). That's some duplication, but rule 4 explicitly says do both for 2-D tables. OK.\n\nShould I also include \"column_units\"? The R137 example includes column_units. Yes, include.\n\nRegarding certificate.scheme: \"A\" — from number. Include.\n\nShould date_issued be \"2021-11-23\"? Format — schema says date_issued; earlier examples presumably ISO. I'll use \"2021-11-23\".\n\nThe `description` and `footnotes` in matrix_tables: schema shows them as fields. Include description: null and footnotes: [] or omit? Schema lists them; I'll include with null/empty or omit. To be safe, include description: null and omit footnotes or empty array. I'll include \"description\": null and \"footnotes\": [].\n\nHmm, actually simpler: include name, columns, column_units, rows. Omit description/footnotes since not applicable (rule 8: omit fields not present). The schema lists them but rule 8 says omit when not present. I'll include just what's present... but description \"not present\" → omit. OK, omit description and footnotes.\n\nActually for the matrix table name: \"Indicating range and verification scale interval by meter size\" — fine.\n\nIssuing authority: include {\"name\": \"NMi\"}. The fragment shows \"NMi\" as a header. Fine.\n\nOne question: should manufacturers include a role note like \"production location\"? The schema doesn't have a role field for manufacturers. I'll just list them. Alternatively I could add a co